erous  she's a woman who will persevere and  provide for all of them despite the grim  circumstances but then again Elijah  knows how all of this works by now the  word of the Lord comes instructs he  obeys the word of God is sure the first  time that this happened the word of God  came to Elijah just after he had  declared that there would be a drought  throughout the land and told him go east  hide yourself by a certain stream there  for I have commanded the Ravens to  provide food for you can you imagine  what Elijah was thinking in that moment  oh great God perfect plan but apparently  he couldn't come up with a better one  because he did go and it all unfolded  just says God said it's as if God was  speaking reality into being so this time  around Elijah has a little more  confidence I'm sure in the Word of God  go I've appointed a woman look there's  the woman and so he gets there and he  knows that she's been appointed by God  he knows it he trusts it and he pushes  it to the point of absurdity he asks her  go and get me a little bit of water and  then he says and bring me a little bit  of bread and when she says I have a  handful of flour that I'm about to cook  for my son and I we're going to eat it  and we're going to die he says sure sure  sure do exactly what you just said only  make a little bit for me first  and then make something for you and your  son it will all be fine don't be afraid  she has been appointed by God and Elijah  knows it but nobody told her the Word of  God is not coming clearly ringing in her  ears with step-by-step instructions and  words of assurance she's just out one  morning collecting firewood and she  comes across this poor beggar now  remember that Elijah has been out in the  woods for months as the Ravens provide  him food day by day in the morning in  the evening and so there's no halo of  light around his head there's no parting  of the heavens as the Word of God or the  finger of God points down and announces  him as the prophet of the Lord there's  just this guy who's been living in the  woods for months and looks and smells  like he's been living in the woods for  months also on top of that he's clearly  a foreigner he doesn't look like her he  doesn't talk like her in fact she knows  right away that he's an Israelite how he  came to be in her town she has no idea  so when he asks her water she complies  without a word but when he pushes  further she scoffs at him and his  response is kind of crazy you know he  says sure sure do what you just said  only make me a little bit first first he  comforts her do not be afraid then he  demands that she provide for him before  she provides for herself or her own son  and then he prophesized for thus says  the Lord the meal shall not lack the oil  shall not be spent until the day that  the Lord brings rain onto the earth this  is not her God she knows nothing of the  God of Israel the story rushes forward  we know that she goes and does exactly  what Elijah says but is worth pausing  for a moment to consider that she had a  few other options at this point she's  sir sizing her own agency God's will is  not her destiny she's making difficult  choices in this moment she doesn't say I  don't know you she could have gone home  and she could have closed the door she  could have come up with any number of  excuses for why it was wiser more  reasonable safer for her to just ignore  him she could have cursed him for not  preparing a little bit better to provide  for himself the way she has been  struggling to do for herself in her own  family through this time of trial she  doesn't do any of those things the other  thing she doesn't do one of the other  things that she doesn't do I'm sure  there are many she doesn't say my family  comes first and i think this one is  actually much harder than the first  because her decisions affect not only  her own life but the well-being of her  son and so she could have said i have a  responsibility to my son a